## Your attitude to risk

You completed an Attitude to Risk questionnaire. We felt that this didn't fully reflect your risk appetite. We agreed that you are a risk rating 5 rather than a 4 as per the questionnaire. You are happy to proceed with a Risk rating of 5.

You confirmed that you wish to increase your Risk rating to 5- Balanced investor, you are aware that this is higher than your agreed risk rating and are happy to take on this risk with your pension. You have confirmed that you are not reliant upon your pension funds and wish for them to have the best growth potential over a 10-year period and feel a balanced approach to this investment would achieve this goal. You are aware that your funds may go up as well as down, and the higher risk you take with your funds, potential there is for larger drops in value.

As a Balanced investor, you do not see yourself as a particularly cautious person and have no strong positive or negative associations with the notion of taking risk.  If you have some experience in investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters, then you may be suited to a Balanced approach to investing.  You may also be suited to this approach if you make investment decisions reasonably quickly and don't tend to be particularly anxious about those decisions.  As a Balanced investor, you can be inclined to look for a combination of investments with differing levels of risk and understand that you may need to take some risk to meet your investment goals.

